Round 29 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
  - `clang/aot/_.c`
- Implemented tri-state MAT-DP probe result in `aot_try_mat_dp_ctr_match(...)`:
  - `0`: no fast path
  - `1`: DP payload is constructor with matching `ext` (existing match fast path)
  - `2`: DP payload is constructor with mismatching `ext` (new mismatch fast path)
- Head `MAT` emission now handles probe status `2` by jumping directly to branch-1 (`mat_loc + 1`) without running `aot_force_strict` on the DP scrutinee.
- Added MAT-DP miss telemetry by payload tag for `non_ctr` probes:
  - `AOT_MAT_DP non_ctr_pre[tag=...]`
  - `AOT_MAT_DP non_ctr_post[tag=...]`

Critical bug found and fixed
- Initial implementation of the `probe==2` branch incorrectly consumed the scrutinee argument (`*a_pos--` / `*s_pos--`).
- This violated existing MAT mismatch lowering semantics and caused AOT segfaults (`factorial`, `fibo`, `sum_4`, `use_match_depth`).
- Fix: mismatch fast path must NOT consume the arg; it must mirror the existing generic ext-miss arm behavior exactly.

Why this mattered
- Previous telemetry showed many DP constructor ext-miss probes still paid generic strict forcing and DUP work.
- The new `probe==2` branch removes that avoidable force step while staying deopt-clean.

Validation
- Build: `cd clang && clang -O2 -o main main.c`
- Tests: `./test/_all_.sh` passed after the mismatch-arg fix.
- Canaries (`--as-c -s -T1`, with `HVM_AOT_DEOPT=1 HVM_AOT_HEAP_ATTR=1 HVM_AOT_MAT_DP=1`) stayed deopt-clean (`AOT_DEOPT total=0`).

