Key lessons
- The dominant MAT-DP miss class is nested DP payloads (`tag=3/4`, i.e., `DP0/DP1`) that the current probe does not collapse.
- `non_ctr_post` is effectively absent in sampled canaries; misses are mostly pre-force DP payloads, not failed strict local force conversions.
- Next material gain likely needs DP-on-DP specialization (or another lazy projection composition path), not more ctor ext checks.

